  Server IP 10.38.215.65  = tb470 (the DHCP server)
  VLAN 1 / Port port2.0.9 = the UNTRUSTED access port the client sits behind
  Expiry ~389s            = counts down from the tb470 lease
  Type Dyn                = learned by snooping (not a static binding)
VERIFY: binding database has correct values. PASS.

================================================================================
NOTES
================================================================================
- Binding is CREATED when the snooper pairs the client's REQUEST ingressing an untrusted
  port with the server's ACK arriving on the trusted port. The switch's OWN SVI client
  would lease but NOT bind (its lease lives in `show dhcp lease`, not the snooping table) —
  which is why a genuine downstream host (the x230) is required for Step 3.
- On first attempt the stale vlan50 binding from an earlier isolated-island run persisted
  in nvs and the fresh lease raced the interface read; `clear ip dhcp snooping binding`
  plus a clean re-lease produced the correct single vlan1 entry above.
- All config is running-config only (reverts on reload). Snooping is a transient test
  overlay on the clean bench; bench-state.md/tb470.setup record the clean baseline itself.
